PAGE MSG-VIEW
TITLE Reading a message
KIND screen
SCREENS MSG-VIEW
HELP Left/Right tabs  k QSL  x processed  t tag  T transmit  ? guide
KEY Left/Right Moves between the tabs: TEXT, DECODED, EVENTS, PROPS.
KEY k QSL it.
KEY x Marks it processed.
KEY d Discards it.
KEY e Exports it.
KEY t Adds your own tag to it, a note only this station sees.
KEY E Edits a corrected copy. The message as received is kept.
KEY y Copies the code groups.
KEY T Sends it on (asks first, No by default): keys the radio.
SEE MSG-INBOX MSG-OUTBOX EMCON
BEGIN_TEXT
TEXT is the message as it came over the air. DECODED shows an enciphered
message in the clear, when this station holds the key; otherwise it says
there is no key here. EVENTS is its history, oldest first. PROPS lists
precedence, key name (never the key itself), source, destination, ALE
address, data rate and checksum.

T is the only key on this screen that transmits. It names the route and
asks first. While EMCON is on, nothing goes out.
END
